---
import BusyForms from "~/components/BusyForms.astro";
import Theme from "~/components/Theme.astro";
import { APP_NAME, INVITE_TTL_DAYS, operator } from "~/config";
import "~/styles/global.css";

export const prerender = false;

/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Describes exactly what the schema in `src/db/schema.ts` stores — if you add
 * fields to the application, add them here too. A policy that does not match
 * what the system does is worse than none.
 *
 * This is an honest base text, not legal advice. If your case involves
 * sensitive data, minors or international transfers, have it reviewed.
 */
const OPERATOR = operator(Astro.locals.env);
const updated = "September 17, 2026";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <title>Privacy Policy — {APP_NAME}</title>
    <Theme />
    <BusyForms />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="doc">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">{APP_NAME} · updated on {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This page explains what data {APP_NAME} stores about you, why it stores it,
        for how long, and what you can demand in that regard.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {OPERATOR.name} — contact: <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.contact}`}>{OPERATOR.contact}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Where it comes from</th><th>What for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Name</td><td>you provide it, or it comes from the social login provider</td><td>identifying you in the interface</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email</td><td>you provide it when creating the account, or it comes from the social login provider</td><td>login, password recovery, account notices</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Phone</td><td>you provide it, if you want</td><td>optional; contact</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Password</td><td>you set it</td><td>authentication — stored only as a hash, never in plain text</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2FA secret and recovery codes</td><td>generated when you enable it</td><td>second factor — stored encrypted</td></tr>
          <tr><td>IP address and browser</td><td>from your requests</td><td>active sessions and audit trail</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Action log</td><td>what you do in the system</td><td>security: knowing who changed what and when</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Social account identifier</td><td>Google or GitHub, if you use them</td><td>linking the social login to your account</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Workspaces you belong to, and your role in each one</td><td>from whoever created the workspace or invited you</td><td>deciding what you can see and do in each workspace</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        When you log in with Google or GitHub, we receive <strong>only</strong> your name, email
        and profile picture. We have no access to the contents of your account on those services.
      </p>

      <h2>For how long</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Sessions</strong> expire in 7 days, and you can end them before that under Security.</li>
        <li><strong>Invites</strong> expire in {INVITE_TTL_DAYS} days.</li>
        <li><strong>Audit records</strong> are preserved for as long as the account exists. They are
            precisely what makes it possible to investigate improper access, so they are not deleted on request.</li>
        <li><strong>Your account data</strong> stays for as long as the account exists.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        With no one for commercial purposes. We do not sell data and we do not use advertising.
        The data lives on Cloudflare's infrastructure, and the system's emails go out through an
        email delivery provider. These vendors process the data only to deliver the service.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Brazil's LGPD (Law 13,709/2018) you can request, at any time: confirmation that
        we process your data, access to it, correction of anything that is wrong, and the deletion
        of your account. Write to <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.contact}`}>{OPERATOR.contact}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        An honest caveat about deletion: we delete your account data, but we preserve the
        audit trail in dissociated form. It exists for the security of everyone in the system,
        and deleting it would open a hole precisely where it would matter most.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Passwords are stored as hashes. The 2FA secret and the recovery codes are
        encrypted. All traffic goes over HTTPS. Creating an account requires confirming the
        email, and each workspace is accessible only to those who were invited to it.
      </p>

      <p class="muted"><small><a href="/login">Back to login</a></small></p>
    </main>

    <style>
      .doc { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 20px 80px; }
      .doc h1 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
      .doc h2 { margin: 32px 0 10px; font-size: 1rem; }
      .doc p, .doc li { line-height: 1.65; }
      .doc ul { padding-left: 20px; }
      .doc li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
      .doc table { margin: 12px 0 20px; }
      .doc td, .doc th { white-space: normal; vertical-align: top; }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
